      "final_text": "I built the five-page Acme Notes site as one push, which has linked. I've declared T1 done, but its acceptance check (`python -m pytest -q`) hasn't reported back yet. It passed locally (3 tests) before I pushed.\n\nI did the whole task myself without splitting it into subtasks, because it was small.\n\n- **Nav:** it links all five pages in the required order. I changed `build.py` so each built page's own nav link gets `aria-current=\"page\"`, and no other link does.\n- **Pages:** the five fragments in `pages/` follow the spec for each page.\n- **Styles:** `styles.css` styles every required class and the current nav link, with a layout under `@media (max-width: 700px)`.\n- **Tests:** I added `tests/test_site.py`. It builds the site and checks the nav, titles, local links and page content.\n\nThe contact form's `action` is `mailto:hello@acme.example`. The About page's team names (Ada Lovelace, Grace Hopper, Alan Turing) and its company story are placeholders I made up.",
